[Audio:weapon-pop:Weapon Pop]
Played by #R$A445.
Forty clicks, whose half periods come from a counter that goes down by two
each time. This is an example, as the number of clicks depends on #R$5E25
(here it is #N$03).

#AUDIO0(weapon-pop.wav)(#INCLUDE(WeaponPop))

[Audio:appearing-sound:Appearing Sound]
Played by #R$A45F, once for each row of the player that is drawn as the
player appears. This is the sound for the knight, whose sprite is #N$12 rows
high, so the steps are for rows #N$01 to #N$11.

#AUDIO0(appearing-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(AppearingSound))

In the game each step is played on a separate pass of the main loop, so the
steps are further apart than they are here.

